course: dictionary
lesson: 4938
title: Important
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Important» means mattering a lot, or having a big effect or value. «It is important to show your working» tells you that your working matters, so you must not skip it.
explain: An important person has power or is respected. «An important message» means a message that needs attention now. The words around the word show you which meaning fits.
explain: Look for signal words such as «the most important thing» or «the most important part». They tell you what matters most, so you can focus on it.
fact: Important means mattering a lot, or having a big effect or value.
fact: An important person has power or is respected.
fact: «Important» can mean needing attention now, as in «an important message».
fact: «The most important» means more important than anything else.
fact: Important changes to more important and most important when you compare things.
exercise: «It is important to show your working.» What does important mean here? | Hard to see | *Mattering a lot, so you should not skip it | Given away free | Very loud
exercise: «Daydreaming is a normal part of thinking, as long as you are not missing something important, like a road to cross.» Why is a road to cross important? | *It has a big effect on your safety | It is a colour | It is always green | It is very long
exercise: Mia says «an important message» is a message from a famous person. What does important really suggest? | *Needs attention now | Is always long | Is written in pencil | Is from a famous person only
test: «The most important thing» tells the listener what? | Ignore this part | *Pay the most attention to this | It is a joke | Write this in a song
test: Which word fills the gap in «an ___ message» to mean needing attention now? | *important | quiet | sleepy | green
exam: «The most important part of putting it right is making it right with the person who was punished instead of you.» What does important show here? | Something that is only about colours | Something that happened last week | Something you can skip without a problem | *Something that matters most in the process
